{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>All the livestock of Egypt.</b> That is, they did not bring them in from the field, and therefore it does not say ״which are in the field.״ Understand this." "<b>And of the livestock of the children of Israel.</b> For they had them since the days of Jacob and his sons who came down to Egypt, and perhaps also because they acquired them from the relief they gained during the plague of blood. Further, it may mean that if the Egyptians tried to be cunning by selling to Israel so that they would be called by the name of Israel, so that HaShem would distinguish them and they would not die, and they tried to circumvent — these too died. But the livestock of Israel that are in truth their own livestock did not die. And the reading of the verse is: וַיָּמָת כָּל מִקְנֵה מִצְרַיִם — and one portion of the livestock of the children of Israel. And the meaning of מן is not מן as ״some of the flock,״ but rather מן as ״some of the livestock that was called by the name of Israel״ — for there is livestock that is called by his name and is his, and there is that which is not his but only his name is called upon it. And it says that one category of the livestock of Israel, concerning which the Egyptians had schemed to call them by their name, died. But the livestock of Israel — meaning that which is in truth Israel's — not even one of them died."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:26:04.527469040Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}